.TH BOOMERANGZ 1 "September 2026" "boomerangz" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boomerangz \- property-driven ZFS snapshot and replication manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boomerangz
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boomerangz
manages OpenZFS snapshots, retention, local replication, SSH replication, and
authenticated native replication
from policy stored in ZFS user properties. The daemon runs as an unprivileged
service account with explicitly delegated ZFS permissions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run reconciliation, scheduling, replication, pruning, and inactive-dataset
retirement in the foreground.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon status. Use
.B --watch
to follow changes and
.B --interval
to bound refresh time.
.TP
.B trigger
Queue an immediate snapshot for selected active roots, or all active roots when
no dataset is named.
.TP
.B dataset list
List discovered datasets and their management status. Use
.B --json
for structured output.
.TP
.B dataset inspect DATASET
Inspect one dataset's resolved policy and property provenance. Use
.B --json
for structured output.
.TP
.B dataset adopt DATASET
Preview adoption of an existing lineage. Add
.B --apply
to apply after revalidation.
.TP
.B dataset clean
Preview explicit decommissioning. Selection requires exact dataset arguments,
.BR --recursive ,
or
.BR --all .
Snapshots are retained unless
.B --destroy-owned-snapshots
is supplied. Add
.B --apply
to apply after revalidation.
.TP
.B identity recover
Preview installation-identity recovery from local owner markers. Add
.B --owner
when more than one candidate exists and
.B --apply
to apply.
.TP
.B config check
Validate the primary configuration file, every drop-in, and the merged result.
.TP
.B config show
Print the effective configuration with secrets redacted.
.TP
.B config reload
Validate and atomically apply the running daemon configuration. Use
.B --socket
to select a non-default current control socket. The JSON result identifies
fields applied live and fields requiring restart.
.TP
.B pairing create
Create a one-time pairing bundle for a configured TCP listener. Scopes are
.BR status ,
.BR trigger ,
.BR replicate ,
.BR prune ,
and
.BR admin .
.TP
.B pairing import NAME BUNDLE
Import a pairing bundle under a local credential name.
.TP
.B pairing list
List issued and imported pairings.
.TP
.B pairing revoke ID
Revoke a Boomerangz-managed pairing.
.TP
.B ssh-shell
Serve the restricted replication protocol over standard input and output,
bounded by the
.B ssh_shell.replication_roots
configuration. This command is intended for the packaged restricted login
shell, not interactive use.
.TP
.B version
Show build version, commit, and date. Use
.B --json
for structured output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/boomerangz/config.toml
Primary configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/boomerangz/config.d/*.toml
Lexically ordered configuration drop-ins.
.TP
.I /etc/boomerangz/credentials.d/
Imported client credentials and SSH key material.
.TP
.I /var/lib/boomerangz/identity/
Installation identity, server identity, and token verifiers.
.TP
.I /run/boomerangz/boomerangz.sock
Local daemon control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boomerangz.toml (5),
.BR zfs (8),
.BR zfs-allow (8),
.BR ssh (1)
